<title>MEXICO: Mexico seeks to boost crude exports 8.7 pct in '97.</title>
<headline>Mexico seeks to boost crude exports 8.7 pct in '97.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico intends to boost crude export sales in 1997 by 8.7 percent to 1.704 million barrels per day (bpd) from the 1.569 million bpd that this year is seen averaging.</p>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) made the crude export sales estimate in a report to the Energy Commission of the Chamber of Deputies.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287903.</p>
</text>
